316
01:47:37,240 --> 01:47:57,600
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, papagpatuloy ko lang po. Inusod po yung schedule ng [unclear] po ay pinayagan po ma-reopen para makapagtanong. Dito po sa House, nagre-request po ako ng reopening. Hindi naman po siguro maganda na wala akong nakapagtanong dito sa budget ng House.

317
01:47:57,600 --> 01:47:58,640
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Is it a motion?

318
01:47:58,640 --> 01:48:00,960
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, patapusin lang po.

319
01:48:00,960 --> 01:48:29,980
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Considering po na sa lahat ng sangay ng gobyerno, tayo po ay allowed ng liquidation by certification. So kung allowed po tayo ng liquidation by certification, mas lalong dapat ipaliwanag sa taong bayan papaano po ginagastos yung pera nila dahil hindi naman po natin ito [unclear]. So I'm asking for a motion for reconsideration to reopen the budget of the House and be presented to the plenary in the same way that it was allowed for the MMDA.

320
01:48:30,000 --> 01:48:33,080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With the indulgence of our distinguished colleague,

321
01:48:33,800 --> 01:48:39,000
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: while the proposed budget of the MMDA was indeed reconsidered

322
01:48:39,620 --> 01:48:43,660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: upon the motion of the majority giving way and yielding way

323
01:48:43,660 --> 01:48:47,880
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to the listed members who arrived and who wished their intention to interpolate,

324
01:48:49,180 --> 01:48:52,080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: in the case of the budget of the House of Representatives,

325
01:48:53,160 --> 01:48:57,320
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: it does not mean that the leadership doesn't want to discuss the proposed budget.

326
01:48:57,320 --> 01:48:58,040
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: In fact,

327
01:48:58,860 --> 01:48:59,820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the House is very much...

328
01:49:00,000 --> 01:49:01,660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: very much willing to discuss this.

329
01:49:02,360 --> 01:49:02,780
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: However,

330
01:49:03,420 --> 01:49:04,060
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: if I may,

331
01:49:04,440 --> 01:49:07,420
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and with respectful indulgence to our distinguished colleague,

332
01:49:08,060 --> 01:49:10,840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Section 105 of our rules states,

333
01:49:11,540 --> 01:49:14,800
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: when a measure, report, or motion is approved, adopted, or lost,

334
01:49:15,200 --> 01:49:19,160
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: a member who voted with the majority may move for its reconsideration on the same

335
01:49:19,160 --> 01:49:21,180
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: or succeeding session day.

336
01:49:21,780 --> 01:49:24,040
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: As we have conferred with the Secretary General,

337
01:49:24,660 --> 01:49:27,300
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the Honorable Toby Chanko was on official business,

338
01:49:27,300 --> 01:49:29,580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: on official travel abroad,

339
01:49:30,000 --> 01:49:33,740
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: hence, with due courtesy, Honorable Toby Chanko,

340
01:49:34,880 --> 01:49:37,640
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: your motion for reconsideration is out of order.

341
01:49:37,640 --> 01:49:40,840
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: No, Madam Speaker, it says on the next session day.

342
01:49:41,340 --> 01:49:44,460
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: We are not yet on the next session day because we have not yet adjourned.

343
01:49:44,460 --> 01:49:47,800
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So we are still in the same session day, Madam Speaker.

344
01:49:47,800 --> 01:49:50,160
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So you cannot use that rule, Madam Speaker.

345
01:49:50,160 --> 01:49:52,760
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: It says on the next session day.

346
01:49:52,760 --> 01:49:55,320
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: We are still on the same session day, so it's a continuing session.

347
01:49:55,320 --> 01:49:59,680
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So dapat po kung ganyan ang gusto niyong gamitin na rule, dapat po

348
01:49:59,680 --> 01:50:07,240
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: nag-adjourn po noon para next session day, eh Biyernes at hindi na po ako puwedeng mag-motion for reconsideration ngayon.

349
01:50:07,340 --> 01:50:09,680
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: I am not actually referring to the next session day.

350
01:50:09,980 --> 01:50:15,620
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: I am referring, the presiding officer, referring to a motion for reconsideration of a member

351
01:50:15,620 --> 01:50:19,620
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: who voted with the majority insofar as the motion

352
01:50:19,620 --> 01:50:24,860
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to terminate the period of interpolation of the proposed budget of the Congress of the Philippines.

353
01:50:24,860 --> 01:50:26,200
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Within the next session day.

354
01:50:26,960 --> 01:50:29,480
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Hindi pa po tumadaan yung isang session day, Madam Speaker.

355
01:50:29,500 --> 01:50:29,680
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yes.

356
01:50:29,840 --> 01:50:31,880
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Anyway, just rule on it, Madam Speaker.

357
01:50:32,000 --> 01:50:34,740
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kung talagang hindi kayo papayag, then just rule on it.

358
01:50:35,000 --> 01:50:36,860
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The parliamentary status is this.

359
01:50:37,500 --> 01:50:41,820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The proposed, the interpolations of the proposed budget of the House of Representatives

360
01:50:41,820 --> 01:50:45,060
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: has been terminated as moved by the minority,

361
01:50:45,240 --> 01:50:49,820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: duly seconded by the majority last Thursday, September...

362
01:50:53,480 --> 01:50:57,820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: September 17, 2026 at approximately...

363
01:50:59,840 --> 01:51:00,900
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: before noontime.

364
01:51:01,820 --> 01:51:05,860
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: A motion for reconsideration is being put forwarded by the Honorable Chanko.

365
01:51:06,420 --> 01:51:09,580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: While the presiding officer would gladly yield,

366
01:51:10,100 --> 01:51:14,760
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: unfortunately, our rule states that only a member who had voted with the majority

367
01:51:14,760 --> 01:51:17,220
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: can vote for the reconsideration.

368
01:51:17,380 --> 01:51:19,200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With that, our apologies.

369
01:51:19,920 --> 01:51:22,200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The motion for reconsideration is out of order.

370
01:51:22,460 --> 01:51:22,840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: So ruled.

371
01:51:23,600 --> 01:51:24,420
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, Madam Speaker.

372
01:51:24,420 --> 01:51:28,840
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: But I think more than the rules, transparency is more important than our rules.

373
01:51:28,960 --> 01:51:29,820
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kasi kung gusto po natin,

374
01:51:29,840 --> 01:51:31,460
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: magigilan ng korupsyon,

375
01:51:32,160 --> 01:51:33,360
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: kailangan po may accountability.

376
01:51:33,880 --> 01:51:36,600
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kung wala pong accountability, kung wala pong transparency.

377
01:51:37,200 --> 01:51:39,900
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So, but if that is your rule, then I will respect it.

378
01:51:42,240 --> 01:51:44,140
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Thank you very much, Honorable Chanko.

