2591
04:34:39,020 --> 04:34:54,660
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, higit po nating pag-aaralan ang isusumiteng initial report ng Comelec tungkol dito upang matiyak po natin ang interes ng malayang pagboto at ang pagkakaroon ng halalan na

2592
04:34:54,680 --> 04:35:24,660
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: pantay, na patas at malinis po sa lahat ng mga naghahangad na ito ay buong-buong magtagumpay. Ngayon naman po, tungkol naman sa hindi lang po hiling pero panawagan ng representasyong ito, at nawa?y makasama natin dito ang distinguished sponsor. Napakalaki ho ng budget cut para sa programa na may kinalaman sa online voting para po sa ating mga

2593
04:35:24,660 --> 04:35:54,640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: overseas na voters. Gayundin po, napakababa ng pondo para sa voter information and education program. Ito po yung mga programa na magtitiyak ng tagumpay ng halalan ay hindi po nakadepende lang sa Comelec. Pero magtitiyak na yung tao mismo, ang ating mga kababayan mismo, ay nakakaalam kung paano sila magbabantay at kung paano sila kasama sa pagtitiyak ng

2594
04:35:54,640 --> 04:36:00,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: karapatan sa pagboto at kung paano rin sila kasama sa pagtataguyod ng tunay na demokrasya dito sa ating bansa.

2595
04:36:00,880 --> 04:36:23,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At sana po makasama natin ang distinguished sponsor sa panawagan na ma-restore sa 2026 level ang mga programang ito kung hindi man madagdagan para makahabol po tayo sa target na mas maraming registered voters para sa susunod na halalan. Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker. Maraming salamat, distinguished sponsor.

2596
04:36:23,600 --> 04:36:40,560
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: Maraming salamat sa comment. Thank you, Mr. Speaker, at thank you to our colleague na sumusuporta po sa madagdagan pa yung mga budget na nawala po sa ating komisyon. And we will submit po lahat po ng hinihinging impormasyon ng ating kasamahan. Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

2597
04:36:40,560 --> 04:36:42,200
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Thank you. Majority Leader.

2598
04:36:42,200 --> 04:36:49,280
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Sergio Dagooc of APEC Party-list.

2599
04:36:49,280 --> 04:36:53,920
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Representative Dagooc is recognized. Please proceed.

2600
04:36:53,920 --> 04:37:17,240
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Thank you, Majority Leader. Mr. Speaker, there being no other members from the minority who wanted to interpellate, I move to terminate the period of interpellation and debate on the proposed budget of the Commission on Elections for fiscal year 2027. Mr. Speaker, thank you very much.

2601
04:37:17,240 --> 04:37:18,480
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: What does the House say?

2602
04:37:18,480 --> 04:37:27,960
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: Mr. Speaker, on the part of the majority, we join the minority in the motion to terminate the interpellations on the proposed budget of the Commission on Elections.

2603
04:37:27,960 --> 04:37:42,800
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: There is a joint motion to terminate the interpellations on the proposed budget of the Commission on Elections. Is there any objection? The Chair hears none. The interpellations on the proposed budget of the Commission on Elections are hereby terminated.

2604
04:37:42,800 --> 04:37:44,480
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

2605
04:37:44,480 --> 04:37:45,210
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Majority Leader.

2606
04:37:45,210 --> 04:37:47,720
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: Mr. Speaker, I move to suspend session for a few minutes.

2607
04:37:47,720 --> 04:37:48,560
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Session suspended.

2608
04:41:03,600 --> 04:41:05,880
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Majority Leader.

2609
04:41:05,880 --> 04:41:08,640
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: Mr. Speaker, I move that we now consider

2610
04:41:08,640 --> 04:41:11,760
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: the proposed budget of the Anti-Red Tape Authority.

2611
04:41:11,760 --> 04:41:13,600
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Is there any objection?

2612
04:41:13,600 --> 04:41:14,880
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: The Chair hears none. Motion is approved.

2613
04:41:14,880 --> 04:41:16,240
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Majority Leader.

2614
04:41:16,240 --> 04:41:21,820
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: Mr. Speaker, may we acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials of the Anti-Red Tape Authority.

2615
04:41:22,440 --> 04:41:39,480
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: They are Director General Ernesto Perez, Deputy Director General Lea Salcedo, Deputy Director General Rocco Jod, Echeverry, Deputy Director General Pua Billy Racho.

2616
04:41:39,480 --> 04:41:48,820
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: We acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials from the Anti-Red Tape Authority, headed by Director General Perez.

2617
04:41:49,260 --> 04:41:51,960
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Welcome to the House of Representatives. Majority Leader.

2618
04:41:53,000 --> 04:42:02,160
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: Mr. Speaker, I now move to recognize Representative Isabel L. Sagarbarria of the Second District of Negros Occidental,

2619
04:42:02,400 --> 04:42:10,480
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: Vice Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations, to answer questions on the proposed budget of the Anti-Red Tape Authority.

2620
04:42:10,480 --> 04:42:13,180
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Representative Sagarbarria is recognized. Please proceed.

2621
04:42:14,820 --> 04:42:22,320
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues, it is my honor and privilege to sponsor the proposed budget of the Anti-

2622
04:42:39,480 --> 04:42:55,140
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Sorry, of the Anti-Money Laundering Council, of the Anti-Red Tape Authority, under the House Bill number 10858,

2623
04:42:55,140 --> 04:43:08,120
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: or the Fiscal Year 2027 General Appropriations Bill, amounting to P436,720,000, since its establishment pursuant to Republic Act number 11032,

2624
04:43:08,120 --> 04:43:10,560
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: or the Ease of Doing Business

2625
04:43:10,560 --> 04:43:13,660
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: and Efficient Government Service Delivery Act of 2018,

2626
04:43:14,560 --> 04:43:19,240
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: ARTA has placed a significant role in reducing regulatory burdens,

2627
04:43:19,840 --> 04:43:21,520
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: streamlining government processes,

2628
04:43:22,100 --> 04:43:27,120
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: and encouraging government agencies to adopt more efficient and digitalized systems.

2629
04:43:27,900 --> 04:43:32,400
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: In just 80 years, ARTA has become a vital institution in our bureaucracy,

2630
04:43:33,280 --> 04:43:36,060
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: delivering reforms that simplify processes,

2631
04:43:36,060 --> 04:43:40,420
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: reduce red tape, and strengthen public trust in government.

2632
04:43:41,260 --> 04:43:47,420
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: The proposed budget of ARTA aims to ensure that the authority continues to function effectively,

2633
04:43:48,220 --> 04:43:53,220
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: uphold reforms, and deliver on its mandate to make government services more efficient,

2634
04:43:53,860 --> 04:43:56,020
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: transparent, and citizen-oriented.

2635
04:43:56,980 --> 04:44:02,060
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Its proposed initiatives, including the enhancement of the digital platforms,

2636
04:44:02,060 --> 04:44:06,040
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: the Philippine-based regulation information system,

2637
04:44:06,600 --> 04:44:08,200
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: electronic complaints management,

2638
04:44:08,840 --> 04:44:14,020
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: and other digital-based programs are directed toward making government transactions

2639
04:44:14,020 --> 04:44:18,820
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: more accessible, transparent, and efficient for the Filipino people.

2640
04:44:19,760 --> 04:44:24,080
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: When we strengthen the ARTA anti-red tape authority,

2641
04:44:24,700 --> 04:44:26,440
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: we strengthen the government itself.

2642
04:44:26,680 --> 04:44:33,480
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: To empower ARTA is to empower the entire bureaucracy to serve with speed, fairness, and integrity.

2643
04:44:34,540 --> 04:44:35,380
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Let us remember,

2644
04:44:36,060 --> 04:44:39,560
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: a government that defeats red tape is a government that delivers.

2645
04:44:40,300 --> 04:44:44,080
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: The government that delivers is a government that earns trust.

2646
04:44:44,820 --> 04:44:48,700
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: The government that earns trust is a government that truly serves its people.

2647
04:44:49,600 --> 04:44:50,960
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: In view of the foregoing,

2648
04:44:51,640 --> 04:44:54,500
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: I respectfully seek the support of this honorable house

2649
04:44:54,500 --> 04:44:59,640
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: for the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget of the anti-red tape authority.

2650
04:45:00,000 --> 04:45:06,400
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. This representation is now ready to answer questions from our colleagues.

2651
04:45:07,200 --> 04:45:08,620
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Thank you very much. Majority Leader?

2652
04:45:09,140 --> 04:45:20,760
Rep. Ernesto "Ernix" Dionisio Jr.: Mr. Speaker, I now move to recognize Representative Iris Marie de Mesa Montes of Party List 4K to interpolate the sponsor on the proposed budget of the anti-red tape.

2653
04:45:21,500 --> 04:45:25,880
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Representative Iris Marie de Mesa Montes is recognized. Please proceed.

2654
04:45:25,880 --> 04:45:31,860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Magandang hapon po, Distinguished Sponsor and to the ARTA.

2655
04:45:32,820 --> 04:45:38,920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ilang katanungan lamang po mula sa Kababaihan Kabalikatan para sa Kapakanan at Kaunlaran ng Bayan or 4K.

2656
04:45:40,620 --> 04:45:52,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Una po, your budget, proposed budget for 2027 of 537 million is slightly higher than the current budget, mga around 14 million. Tama po ba?

2657
04:45:54,160 --> 04:45:55,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang itinaas.

2658
04:45:55,880 --> 04:46:06,860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Based on the current year's budget, budget for 2027 is sufficient to perform your mandate of reducing red tape in government.

2659
04:46:10,820 --> 04:46:13,820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: No. No, it is not, no.

2660
04:46:15,440 --> 04:46:21,520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po, what programs will be affected given this decrease in budget specifically?

2661
04:46:24,160 --> 04:46:25,860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: What programs will be affected?

2662
04:46:25,860 --> 04:46:34,080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: What programs will be affected will not be funded, what processes will be compromised, what activities?

2663
04:46:42,800 --> 04:46:43,640
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Okay.

2664
04:46:44,080 --> 04:46:52,100
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: This reduction runs contrary to ARTA's direction of expanding its reach and strengthening the implementation, Republic of 11032.

2665
04:46:52,900 --> 04:46:55,840
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: The proposed cut will constrain ARTA's capacity to assist the government.

2666
04:46:55,860 --> 04:47:05,460
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: The proposed cut will constrain ARTA's capacity to assist and capacitate government agencies in complying with the law directly affecting its mandate to reduce, if not eliminate, red tape in government services.

2667
04:47:06,040 --> 04:47:15,760
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: It will also delay ongoing systems development intended to speed up complaints handling, improve data gathering, and strengthen database security and management.

2668
04:47:16,760 --> 04:47:25,120
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Our regional field offices, we likewise have to scale back orientation and inspection activities because of reduced funding for travel,

2669
04:47:25,120 --> 04:47:29,860
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: fuel, supplies, training, and other operational requirements.

2670
04:47:30,300 --> 04:47:36,380
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Mr. Speaker, these resources needed to translate the law into actual improvements in government services.

2671
04:47:37,040 --> 04:47:41,940
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Reducing them will limit ARTA's ability to deliver the reforms expected of it.

2672
04:47:42,580 --> 04:47:43,820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

2673
04:47:45,660 --> 04:47:53,280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Regarding po sa citizen complaints, how many complaints about red tape did ARTA receive last year for 2025?

2674
04:47:53,280 --> 04:47:54,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Given the total.

2675
04:47:55,120 --> 04:47:58,580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ilan po ang na-resolve within the mandated timeline?

2676
04:48:01,040 --> 04:48:07,760
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Actually, as of 2026, the total cases received was 12,335.

2677
04:48:08,760 --> 04:48:19,880
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: And the resolved cases within the turnaround time is 11,208, which is 90.86%.

2678
04:48:19,880 --> 04:48:22,400
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Mataas po yung resolution rate.

2679
04:48:23,200 --> 04:48:24,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung saka-sakali,

2680
04:48:25,120 --> 04:48:29,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ano man po, ano yung mga five agencies that received the most complaints?

2681
04:48:29,560 --> 04:48:31,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Can you name the top five agencies?

2682
04:48:38,700 --> 04:48:39,260
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Okay.

2683
04:48:39,260 --> 04:48:47,460
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: The ten most complained government-owned and controlled corporations from January 2, August 31, 2026

2684
04:48:47,460 --> 04:48:52,280
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: are the Home Development Mutual Fund, Pag-IBIG, which is the highest,

2685
04:48:52,280 --> 04:49:03,060
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Social Security System, GSIS, PhilHealth, Land Bank of the Philippines, PhilPost,

2686
04:49:04,120 --> 04:49:11,860
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: National Transmission Corporation, Transco, NFA, Intellectual Property Office,

2687
04:49:12,980 --> 04:49:16,440
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Tourism Infrastructure and Enterprise Zone Authority.

2688
04:49:17,140 --> 04:49:21,440
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: These are the ten most complained government-owned and controlled corporations.

2689
04:49:22,280 --> 04:49:26,140
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: And then for the national government agencies,

2690
04:49:26,900 --> 04:49:31,960
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: we have the LTO, BIR, Food and Drug Administration,

2691
04:49:33,060 --> 04:49:37,960
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Philippine Statistics Authority, National Telecommunications Commission,

2692
04:49:38,840 --> 04:49:44,420
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Department of Education, Land Registration Authority, Register of Deeds,

2693
04:49:45,100 --> 04:49:51,180
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Professional Regulation Commission, PRC, Department of Human Settlement and Urban Development,

2694
04:49:51,180 --> 04:49:52,180
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: and the Department of Education.

2695
04:49:52,280 --> 04:50:14,020
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: For local government, we have the government of Quezon City, of Taguig, of Caloocan, of Pasig, Paranaque, Malolos, Manila, San Jose del Monte, Makati, Muntinlupa, and Avao City.

2696
04:50:14,640 --> 04:50:16,000
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Those are all, Mr. Chair.

2697
04:50:16,000 --> 04:50:17,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po.

2698
04:50:17,700 --> 04:50:29,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, lahat po ba, have all agencies already established a public assistance and complaint desk or your ARTA help desk?

2699
04:50:30,280 --> 04:50:37,360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And is it also properly staffed to handle walk-in complaints, increase in feedback?

2700
04:50:38,360 --> 04:50:44,020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, lahat na po, ano pong porsyento ng mga opisinang meron ng ARTA help desk?

2701
04:50:44,400 --> 04:50:45,320
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

2702
04:50:45,320 --> 04:50:47,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, lahat na po meron?

2703
04:50:48,240 --> 04:50:52,620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Minsan po kasi, Mr. Speaker, I've had this experience just last year.

2704
04:50:52,940 --> 04:51:02,720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: In one of the agencies that you mentioned, sa mga nasa top 10, meron po silang ARTA help desk, pero wala pong personnel.

2705
04:51:03,480 --> 04:51:09,840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, yung personnel po, diba, the agency is mandated, sila po dapat ang magpo-provide ng personnel, tama?

2706
04:51:10,280 --> 04:51:11,720
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Yes, the agency, not the ARTA.

2707
04:51:11,720 --> 04:51:17,540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, how does ARTA check kung totoo yung mga help desk na yun ay properly manned talaga?

2708
04:51:17,700 --> 04:51:27,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Because they can always say, yung agency na yan or office na yan has established a help desk, but wala din pong tao yung help desk.

2709
04:51:33,000 --> 04:51:35,640
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Yeah, I hear your frustration.

2710
04:51:36,240 --> 04:51:42,880
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Actually, it's supposed to be under the law, agencies are all required to establish this ACD.

2711
04:51:45,600 --> 04:51:47,040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2712
04:51:47,700 --> 04:51:59,040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yung tanong ko po, Sana, how do you ensure, meron bang routine inspection na ginagawa ang ARTA to ensure that hindi lang help desk kang nandodon?

2713
04:51:59,240 --> 04:52:03,680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Dapat po talaga may tao the whole day to receive complaints?

2714
04:52:04,480 --> 04:52:13,860
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Actually, we have a compliance inspection and I'm sorry of what had happened.

2715
04:52:14,980 --> 04:52:17,400
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Definitely, in the future, they will be doing that.

2716
04:52:17,700 --> 04:52:19,420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay. Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2717
04:52:20,680 --> 04:52:26,240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Also, have all agencies established the Committee on Anti-Red Tape or yung CART?

2718
04:52:26,580 --> 04:52:29,620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Lahat din po ba meron ng CART sa lahat ng opisina?

2719
04:52:30,400 --> 04:52:36,840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito po yung nag-I understand, yung nag-o-oversee po ng compliance with ARTA rules in each agency.

2720
04:52:37,460 --> 04:52:40,960
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: And if, actually, if they're not compliant, they will be liable.

2721
04:52:40,960 --> 04:52:49,900
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: As of the present, the compliance rate is 70%.

2722
04:52:49,900 --> 04:52:57,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ah, 70%. So, ano pa pong agency? So, madami-dami pa pong walang CART sa mga agencies nila.

2723
04:52:58,720 --> 04:53:05,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, what will we do in order to force them to establish the CART?

2724
04:53:05,460 --> 04:53:10,280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Because it is a mandate under the ease of doing business law.

2725
04:53:10,960 --> 04:53:21,440
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: They will be issued notices to explain.

2726
04:53:22,640 --> 04:53:25,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay. Thank you, Mr. Chair. Madam Sponsor.

2727
04:53:26,180 --> 04:53:30,720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Meron na rin po ba, lahat din po bang agencies, meron ng Citizens Charter?

2728
04:53:33,580 --> 04:53:35,580
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

2729
04:53:35,580 --> 04:53:37,580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Have we issued...

2730
04:53:38,240 --> 04:53:40,800
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: 98% compliance.

2731
04:53:40,960 --> 04:53:42,020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: 98%.

2732
04:53:42,020 --> 04:53:49,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Have we ensured that of this 98% to have complied with the Citizens Charter requirement,

2733
04:53:49,900 --> 04:53:53,020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ay talaga pong sinusunod yung Citizens Charter?

2734
04:53:53,280 --> 04:53:55,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi pwede rin pong compliance lang.

2735
04:53:55,900 --> 04:54:01,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, how can ARTA find out? Do we find out which ones are just complying

2736
04:54:01,660 --> 04:54:05,740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: or which ones are following the Citizens Charter to the letter?

2737
04:54:05,740 --> 04:54:05,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you.

2738
04:54:10,960 --> 04:54:22,160
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: We require them to submit annual updating of the compliance.

2739
04:54:23,100 --> 04:54:24,180
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2740
04:54:24,200 --> 04:54:25,740
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: We conduct inspection also.

2741
04:54:25,780 --> 04:54:31,220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Sponsor, pagdating naman po sa mga investigations and cases,

2742
04:54:31,220 --> 04:54:40,520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: how many show cause orders or cases were initiated against agencies or airing officials that violated the ease of doing business law?

2743
04:54:46,800 --> 04:54:47,300
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Okay.

2744
04:54:48,300 --> 04:54:53,160
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: ARTA investigated a total of 600 cases, Mr. Chair.

2745
04:54:53,300 --> 04:55:01,480
